# Exception patterns for Drupal applications: an error line that also matches any of these
# is not an error. Case-insensitive regular expressions, one per line.
# Ported from dockworker-drupal's DrupalDeployCommands::provideErrorLogConfiguration().

# Drupal 11 local: expected.
Access denied for user 'drupal'
# Drupal 10: a module, not an error.
inline_form_errors
# Drupal 10: expected.
Config language.entity.en does not exist
# Migrate processes reporting 0 failed. The leading space is significant.
[ ]0 failed
# Drupal 9 local: expected.
Operation CREATE USER failed
# Composer summary output.
failure: 0
# Composer suggest output.
error-handler instead
# .well-known trolling.
\.well-known
# Calendar template name.
HoursCalendarUnavailableTemplate
# Drush auto-answers "yes" to a non-fatal requirements check and continues.
Do you wish to continue\?: yes
# Drupal-core config-schema warning prose. Schema warnings are '[warning]'-level and so are
# not scanned, but Drush wraps long ones across lines, leaving unmarked continuation lines.
# The wrap-tails are anchored so a genuine "...failed with errors:" line is never excepted.
following errors:\s*$
(\||^)\s*errors:\s*$
These errors mean there
is configuration that does not comply with its schema
does not comply with its schema
not a fatal error, but it is
recommended to fix these issues
missing schema
